# Lifeblood speech: conversation. The format and every fact and word are described in basics.speech.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Greetings: a player walks up.

== greet ==
It's my birthday today!      {birthday=yes, w=8}
[hello] Guess whose birthday it is? Mine! {birthday=yes, extrovert, w=8}
Oh! Hi. It's, um... my birthday. {birthday=yes, introvert, w=8}
[hello_named]
[hello_named] [smalltalk_short] {w=0.6}
[hello_named] Still in one piece, I see. {opinion=friend}
[listener]! There you are.   {opinion=close_friend, w=2}
There you are, love.         {listener_kin=spouse, w=6}
Hello, dear.                 {listener_kin=spouse, polite, w=5}
Oh! It's you. Hi.            {listener_kin=partner, introvert, w=6}
Hey, you.                    {listener_kin=partner, w=5}
There's my favorite person.  {listener_kin=partner, romantic, w=6}
Hello, future spouse! Too much? Too much. {listener_kin=fiance, lighthearted, w=4}
Hello, soon-to-be.           {listener_kin=fiance, w=5}
Oh, it's you. Good.          {opinion=friend}
...                          {opinion=disliked}
Oh. It's you.                {opinion=disliked}
Keep walking.                {opinion=disliked, rude}
What do you want?            {opinion=disliked, rude+}
Hm. Hello.                   {opinion=disliked, polite}
Hey, [listener]. Coming along? {leader=yes}
Right behind you.            {leader=yes}
Mm.                          {taciturn, w=2}
[hello] Lovely weather for ducks. {weather=rain, lighthearted}
[hello] Miserable weather.   {weather=rain, pessimist}
[hello] Some rain, huh?      {weather=rain}
[hello] Isn't this rain wonderful? {weather=rain, weather_like=love}
[hello] Get inside, it's pouring. {weather=rain, weather_like=hate, outside=yes}
[hello] Some storm, huh?     {weather=storm}
[hello] Hear that thunder?   {weather=storm, weather_like=love}
Oh, thank goodness, company. This storm... {weather=storm, timid}
[hello] Snow!                {weather=snow, weather_like=love}
[hello] Cold enough for you? {weather=snow, lighthearted}
[hello] Can't see a thing in this fog. {weather=fog}
[hello] Lovely day, isn't it? {weather=clear, weather_like=love, time=day}
[hello] Don't look at the sky. Just don't. {weather=blood_rain}
Oh, hey. Didn't see you there. {timid}
[hello] Need something?      {polite}
[hello] Make it quick.       {rude}
[hello] Make it quick, I'm working. {hardworking, rude}
Oh good, an excuse to stop working. {lazy, lighthearted}
# Family: children and their parents, siblings, grandparents
Hi, [kin_call].              {age=adult, listener_kin=parent, w=8}
Oh, [kin_call]! Good to see you. {age=adult, listener_kin=parent, w=6}
Oh. It's you.                {listener_kin=sibling, w=4}
Hey, trouble.                {listener_kin=sibling, w=6}

== smalltalk_short ==
How's it going?
Keep safe out there.
Nice day.                    {weather=clear, time=day}
Nice day, if you like that sort of thing. {weather=clear, time=day, weather_like=dislike}
Lovely rain.                 {weather=rain, weather_like=love}
Wet one.                     {weather=rain}
Wild weather.                {weather=storm}
Cold out.                    {weather=snow}
Foggy.                       {weather=fog}
Rough day.                   {mood=bad}
What a day!                  {mood=great}

