# The conversation menu

== about_me ==
Me? Not much to tell.
What do you want to know?
Oh! Where do I start?        {extrovert, w=2}
Me? Why?                     {paranoid, w=2}
I'm not very interesting.    {humble, w=2}
Finally, someone asks.       {proud, w=2}
Ugh. Fine.                   {rude}
Hm.                          {taciturn, w=2}
That's a big question.       {serious}
I'm an open book. A short one. {lighthearted}
[name] [family_name], at your service. {polite, w=2}
I'm a [family_name]. That tells you most of it. {proud, w=2}
The [family_name]s have always been decent folk. {sentimental, w=2}
I was a [birth_family_name] before I married. {married_name=yes, w=3}

== where_from ==
[home_biome.the.cap]. Born and raised. {w=3}
[home_biome.the.cap]. You can probably tell. {w=2}
I'm from [home_biome.the]. {w=3}
[home_biome.the.cap]. Best place there is. {biome_like=like, at_home=yes, w=2}
Right here! [home_biome.the.cap], born and raised. {at_home=yes, w=4}
You're standing in it. [home_biome.the.cap]. {at_home=yes, lighthearted, w=3}
Here. Never been anywhere else, really. {at_home=yes, introvert, w=3}
Oh, [home_biome.the]! I could talk about it for hours. Don't worry, I won't. {extrovert, w=2}
[home_biome.the.cap]. Why? {paranoid, w=3}
Why do you want to know? {paranoid, w=1}
[home_biome.the.cap]. Not that it's any of your business. {rude, w=3}
[home_biome.the.cap].        {taciturn, w=4}
[home_biome.the.cap]. Cold enough to freeze the words in your mouth. {home_climate=cold, w=3}
[home_biome.the.cap]. You learn to love snow, or you leave. {home_climate=cold, w=2}
[home_biome.the.cap]. You learn to love the heat, or you leave. {home_climate=hot, w=2}
[home_biome.the.cap]. Hot as hell and twice as dry. {home_climate=hot, crude, w=3}
[home_biome.the.cap]. Not much to say about it. It's nice. {home_climate=mild, w=2}
[home_biome.the.cap]. Haven't been back in a long time. {at_home=no, serious, w=2}
[home_biome.the.cap]. I miss it. {at_home=no, w=2}
[home_biome.the.cap]. I don't miss it. {at_home=no, pessimist, w=2}
Around. Here and there.
I'd rather not say.          {taciturn}

== ask_about_who ==
Who?
Who do you mean?
About who?
Ooh. Who?                    {nosy, w=3}
Gossip? I'm listening.       {nosy, w=2}
I don't talk about people behind their backs. {honest, w=2}
Careful what you ask, [listener]. {paranoid}

== opinion_of_you ==
You? You're all right.       {opinion=neutral}
I don't really know you yet. {opinion=neutral}
Honestly? Haven't made my mind up. {opinion=neutral, honest}
I like you, [listener].      {opinion=friendly}
I enjoy having you around.   {opinion=friendly}
You're a friend. A real one. {opinion=friend}
I'd trust you with my life.  {opinion=close_friend}
You're the best friend I've got, [listener]. {opinion=close_friend, w=2}
Honestly? Not much.          {opinion=disliked}
You really want to know? No. {opinion=disliked, rude}
I'd rather not say.          {opinion=disliked, polite}
I can't stand you.           {opinion=enemy}
Get out of my sight.         {opinion=enemy, rude}
You know exactly what I think of you. {opinion=enemy, vengeful}
I think you're wonderful. Don't let it go to your head. {opinion=close_friend, lighthearted}
Do you really need me to say it? {opinion=friend, introvert}

== opinion_of ==
[other]? Don't know much about them.     {about=neutral}
[other]? They're all right.              {about=neutral}
[other]? Haven't made up my mind.        {about=neutral}
[other]? Never really talked.            {about=neutral, introvert}
[other]? Nice enough.                    {about=friendly}
[other]'s good company.                  {about=friendly}
[other]? I like them.                    {about=friendly}
[other]? A good friend.                  {about=friend}
[other] and I go way back. Well. Back.   {about=friend, lighthearted}
I'd do anything for [other].             {about=close_friend}
[other]? My best friend. Don't tell them I said that. {about=close_friend}
[other]? Ugh.                            {about=disliked}
Don't get me started on [other].         {about=disliked}
[other] and I don't get along.           {about=disliked, polite}
[other] is a waste of good air.          {about=disliked, rude}
[other]? I'd rather not say.             {about=disliked, polite}
[other] can go to hell.                  {about=enemy, crude, w=2}
If I never see [other] again, it'll be too soon. {about=enemy}
I'll get [other] one day. You'll see.    {about=enemy, vengeful}
[other]? Don't trust them. Don't trust anyone. {paranoid, w=0.5}
Oh, I have SO much to tell you about [other]. {nosy, about=neutral}
Oh, I have SO much to tell you about [other]. {nosy, about=disliked}
Why, what have you heard about [other]? {nosy, w=0.7}
[other] is my friend. That's all you need to know. {loyal, about=friend}

== never_mind ==
Oh. All right.
Never mind, then.
Hm. Okay.
Make up your mind.           {rude}
Of course.                   {polite}

== follow_accept ==
Lead the way.
Sure, I'll come.
Right behind you.
Let's go!                    {extrovert}
Adventure! Finally!          {curious, w=2}
For you? Of course.          {opinion=friend}
For you, [listener], anywhere. {opinion=close_friend}
I'll watch your back.        {brave}
I'll... try to keep up.      {timid}
Fine, but you're carrying the heavy stuff. {lazy, w=2}
Can't let you go alone.      {loyal, w=2}
The Cube God guide our steps. {pious}
Ha! Let's see what's out there. {lighthearted}
If we must.                  {pessimist}
Anywhere with you, [kin_call]. {listener_kin=parent, w=6}
Where you go, I go.          {listener_kin=spouse, w=6}

== follow_refuse ==
I don't think so.
No, thank you.
I'd rather stay here.
I hardly know you.           {opinion=neutral}
Why would I go anywhere with you? {opinion=disliked, w=2}
Not a chance.                {opinion=disliked, rude, w=2}
Not with you. Never with you. {opinion=enemy, w=2}
Sorry, I'm a homebody.       {introvert}
And walk all that way? No.   {lazy, w=2}
I've got work to do here.    {hardworking, w=2}
Ask me again when I know you better. {polite, opinion=neutral}
How do I know you won't lead me into a trap? {paranoid, w=2}
I'm in no shape to go anywhere. {recovering=yes, w=5}
Hell no.                     {crude, opinion=disliked}
Maybe some other time.       {polite}
Sorry, [kin_call]. Not today. {listener_kin=parent, w=6}
Not today, love.             {listener_kin=spouse, w=6}

== follow_stop ==
All right. I'll head home.
Fair enough. Be safe.
Oh. Okay.
Aw. That was fun.            {extrovert}
Finally. My feet are killing me. {lazy, w=2}
Back to work, then.          {hardworking}
Call me if you need me, [listener]. {opinion=friend}
Fine. Don't miss me too much. {lighthearted}
Was it something I said?     {sentimental}

== follow_quit ==
You know what? I'm done following you.
I've had enough of you, [listener]. I'm going home.
That's it. Find someone else to follow.
I'm not following you anywhere anymore.
Go on without me. Far without me.     {rude}
I'm sorry, [listener]. I can't do this anymore. {polite}
To hell with this. I'm out.           {crude, w=2}
I'll remember this, [listener].       {vengeful}
I thought we were friends.            {sentimental, w=2}

== practical_open ==
What do you need?
Business, then.
Sure. What is it?
Go on.
At your service.             {polite, proper}
Make it quick.               {rude}
Practical stuff. My favorite. {hardworking}
Ugh, practical stuff.        {lazy}
What do you need, [kin_call]? {listener_kin=parent, w=5}
What do you need, love?      {listener_kin=spouse, w=5}

== farewell ==
Bye.
See you around.
Take care.
Later.
Farewell, [listener].        {proper}
Stay safe out there, [listener]. {polite}
Cube God keep you.           {pious, w=2}
Don't let the monsters bite. {lighthearted}
Finally.                     {opinion=disliked, rude}
Hm.                          {taciturn}
Already? Aw.                 {extrovert}
See you, [address].
[taught_farewell]!           {w=3}
[taught_farewell], [listener]. {w=3}
Love you, [kin_call].        {listener_kin=parent, w=6}
Take care of yourself, [kin_call]. {age=adult, listener_kin=parent, w=6}
See you at home, love.       {listener_kin=spouse, w=8}
Come home safe.              {listener_kin=spouse, w=6}
Later. Don't do anything I wouldn't. {listener_kin=sibling, w=5}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trying to talk to them mid-fight, or when they're out to get you. fighting_you=yes when you're who they're
# fighting; in_combat=no means they're hostile but not fighting yet (say, you're in creative).

== busy_fighting ==
Not now!
Kind of busy here!
Can't talk!
Later!
Not now, [listener]! Help me!  {relation=ally, w=3}
Wait your turn!              {brawling=yes, fighting_you=no, w=4}
This is between me and them. {brawling=yes, fighting_you=no, w=4}
Talking won't save you. Fists up! {brawling=yes, fighting_you=yes, w=6}
